# `GO` at the `)` prompt, and then listen.
#
# This is `restore.script` with its ending changed, and the two endings are
# alternatives rather than a sequence: `008860-A03` Chapter 1 Step 4 says `GO`
# "starts the DM and the login prompt appears", while `shut` dismounts and stops.
# A run can do one or the other.
#
# **It deliberately expects nothing after `GO`.** What the DS5500 prints once the
# DM starts has never been seen on this core, and an `expect` for a prompt this
# project has not read is a guess that costs a whole run when it is wrong --
# `console-script-expect-is-edge-triggered`, twice. So this script ends by
# sending `GO` and lets the console recorder capture whatever follows; the
# dialogue is written from the transcript, not before it.
#
# Pair it with a generous `--boot-limit` and **no** `--boot-stop-on-script-end`:
# the point of this run is the part *after* the last step.
expect MD14
expect >
send DI C\r
expect >
send EX DOMAIN_OS\r
expect Do you wish to proceed
send Y\r

# RBAK's Phase II banner on the way out, which occurs exactly once in a run --
# `RBAK_BS` at the start is a different string.
expect RBAK version
send GO\r
